WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.080
Tan Daoji's military achievements were outstanding; he was deeply loved by his soldiers and held great prestige at court.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:18.062
But his achievements were too great, and they aroused the court's suspicion. When Emperor Wen fell gravely ill, some worried that Tan Daoji would be hard to control afterwards.

00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:30.172
The court ordered Tan Daoji to be put to death. When he was arrested, he said angrily: You are destroying your own Great Wall!

00:00:30.522 --> 00:00:34.602
When the soldiers heard the news, they all felt it was deeply unjust.

00:00:34.952 --> 00:00:41.744
After Tan Daoji's death, the northern frontier no longer had a great general like him to guard it.

00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:47.350
There was not a single person on the wall — only the banners fluttering in the wind.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:54.348
Before long, the Northern Wei army invaded southward, and the Song army retreated again and again.

00:00:54.698 --> 00:01:01.130
Only then did Emperor Wen think of Tan Daoji; his heart was full of regret, but sadly it was already too late.

